WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.274 --> 00:00:03.248
- Now this my friends, is what we used,

00:00:03.248 --> 00:00:05.331
phew, the old, old times.

00:00:06.395 --> 00:00:07.652
What's up, peeps?

00:00:07.652 --> 00:00:10.235
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.479 --> 00:00:19.137
- So, I think these are for the cameras,

00:00:19.137 --> 00:00:21.754
and you put these in front of the cameras,

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:23.217
and you do it like this.

00:00:23.217 --> 00:00:25.382
(upbeat music)

00:00:25.382 --> 00:00:26.880
- Interesting.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.428
- Does this, like, hold discs?

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:29.376
- Tiles?

00:00:29.376 --> 00:00:31.959
(upbeat music)

00:00:34.539 --> 00:00:36.585
(beep)

00:00:36.585 --> 00:00:37.771
- What?

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.199
- It's like this walkie talkie.

00:00:39.199 --> 00:00:40.336
The old walkie talkie.

00:00:40.336 --> 00:00:41.374
(beep)

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.399
What's up, guy?

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:45.918
These walkie talkies are for detectives.

00:00:45.918 --> 00:00:49.041
- Oh, this maybe was used for the army?

00:00:49.041 --> 00:00:49.874
(beep)

00:00:49.874 --> 00:00:51.624
- It's like an alarm.

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:55.349
- It's easier to use than a cell phone,

00:00:55.349 --> 00:00:57.999
'cause then you have your contacts.

00:00:57.999 --> 00:00:59.883
You can just press your contact button

00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:01.724
and then you just call your friend.

00:01:01.724 --> 00:01:04.307
(upbeat music)

00:01:11.276 --> 00:01:14.693
- I figured that this would go into here.

00:01:16.149 --> 00:01:18.982
- How do you think these get in?

00:01:18.982 --> 00:01:21.262
- You put it inside and then you can,

00:01:21.262 --> 00:01:24.512
like, in the morning you can hear news.

00:01:27.899 --> 00:01:29.526
- This is something you definitely use

00:01:29.526 --> 00:01:31.662
to watch something.

00:01:31.662 --> 00:01:35.005
- Oh, I can explore inside of it.

00:01:35.005 --> 00:01:36.237
- How do you get the tape out?

00:01:36.237 --> 00:01:37.570
Oh, there it is.

00:01:39.352 --> 00:01:41.122
- That's complicated.

00:01:41.122 --> 00:01:43.318
I just press a button and boom.

00:01:43.318 --> 00:01:45.985
(playful music)

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:53.057
- This is a phone, you
use this to call people.

00:01:53.057 --> 00:01:56.063
This is, like, a really old one.

00:01:56.063 --> 00:01:57.054
- Hello?

00:01:57.054 --> 00:01:59.814
- In the back old days
you used to put it up

00:01:59.814 --> 00:02:04.142
to your ear and you
have to use, like, this

00:02:04.142 --> 00:02:05.308
to get the number.

00:02:05.308 --> 00:02:06.879
- What if it's an emergency?

00:02:06.879 --> 00:02:08.261
Like, what if someone's robbing your house

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.178
and you do, like, nine.

00:02:13.052 --> 00:02:14.502
Nope, nope, wrong.

00:02:14.502 --> 00:02:16.136
And if you mess up.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:17.361
What do you do if you mess up?

00:02:17.361 --> 00:02:19.694
- I feel so mad for Madonna.

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:21.656
She's old.

00:02:21.656 --> 00:02:23.683
Madonna has to use this type of phone.

00:02:23.683 --> 00:02:25.265
Sorry Madonna.

00:02:25.265 --> 00:02:26.783
I don't know if you're still alive but--

00:02:26.783 --> 00:02:28.533
(laughing)

00:02:28.533 --> 00:02:31.116
(upbeat music)

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.949
- And this is a walkie talkie.

00:02:34.949 --> 00:02:36.687
Oh, it's a cell phone.

00:02:36.687 --> 00:02:38.294
- I think they would call it a flip phone,

00:02:38.294 --> 00:02:39.955
because you, like, flip it

00:02:39.955 --> 00:02:43.125
and then once you have to close it.

00:02:43.125 --> 00:02:43.958
It's like that.

00:02:43.958 --> 00:02:44.791
- Cops use it,

00:02:44.791 --> 00:02:48.396
"Hey, 43, call 43, got
criminals on 92nd street.

00:02:48.396 --> 00:02:49.479
"Go, go, go."

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:52.196
And criminals can use this too.

00:02:52.196 --> 00:02:53.993
"Hey, I just robbed a bank.

00:02:53.993 --> 00:02:55.087
"How we doing?

00:02:55.087 --> 00:02:56.920
"Got stacks of money."

00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:03.134
- Press two once to do a,

00:03:03.134 --> 00:03:05.314
press two twice to do b.

00:03:05.314 --> 00:03:07.390
- That would take forever and ever

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:09.315
and ever and ever.

00:03:09.315 --> 00:03:13.109
- This is, like, what old people use to,

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:14.109
"Hi, honey."

00:03:16.493 --> 00:03:20.163
Yeah, I prefer iPhones,
but these were cool.

00:03:20.163 --> 00:03:22.675
If it's all you have I understand.

00:03:22.675 --> 00:03:26.308
(electronic music)

00:03:26.308 --> 00:03:28.360
- This looks fun.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.277
Tamagotchi.

00:03:30.392 --> 00:03:31.225
- Tam-tam.

00:03:35.012 --> 00:03:36.095
- Tamagotchi.

00:03:38.661 --> 00:03:39.578
Tamagotchi.

00:03:41.557 --> 00:03:43.974
- Yay, my Tamagotchi arrived.

00:03:45.197 --> 00:03:46.095
- I know what these are!

00:03:46.095 --> 00:03:48.231
They're called tamagotchis!

00:03:48.231 --> 00:03:49.072
- That's just boring.

00:03:49.072 --> 00:03:50.066
You just press buttons.

00:03:50.066 --> 00:03:51.679
That's all you do.

00:03:51.679 --> 00:03:55.382
- I'm so glad I was born 2005, modernized.

00:03:55.382 --> 00:03:58.400
I don't want to be born in the 1980s.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.330
I feel bad for my teachers and my parents.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:04.247
(electronic music)

